n access in classroom (water bottle)\n\n3. **FMLA protections**: If she has been employed for 12+ months and her employer has 50+ employees, she is entitled to up to 12 weeks of unpaid, job-protected leave under FMLA. She may also use FMLA intermittently for flare days.\n\n4. **Short-term vs. long-term disability**: If she cannot return to work even with accommodations, document for long-term disability. Include formal neuropsychological testing results, functional capacity assessment, and specialist letters supporting the diagnosis.\n\n**Disability Documentation Tips**:\n- Use objective measures (MoCA scores, 6MWT, CPET results, tilt table results, PFTs) rather than subjective symptoms alone\n- Document treatment adherence and response\n- Describe specific functional limitations in work-relevant terms (\"cannot sustain standing for > 20 minutes,\" \"requires rest breaks every 45 minutes\")\n- Provide clear medical opinion: \"It is my professional medical opinion that this patient is currently unable to perform the essential functions of her job as a full-time classroom teacher without the accommodations listed above.\"',
